{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevPhVjRAt5wsC2E6e9hA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough context. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add an `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` states. Add a `status: OrderStatus` field to the `Order` data class, initially set to `ACTIVE` for new orders.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Update the `create` endpoint to set `status = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` when creating orders. Add a new `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint (`cancelOrder` method) that:\n   - Looks up the order (404 if not found)\n   - If already cancelled, return the order (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with new error code and do nothing\n   - Otherwise, mark order as CANCELLED and update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Return the updated order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add a `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the `create` endpoint, before saving the shipment, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED. If it is, throw ConflictException with new error code.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add two new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` — when cancelling an order blocked by a confirmed shipment\n   - `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` — when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an active order returns 200 with updated status\n   - Cancelling a cancelled order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling an order with a confirmed shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - Created shipments are transitioned to CANCELLED when order is cancelled\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test:\n   - Creating a shipment for a cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Instead of adding a `status` field to Order, could have used a separate OrderStatus table/repository. Rejected because: (1) The requirement says to add status to orders, (2) complexity and in-memory storage patterns in this codebase suggest keeping data together, (3) no existing precedent for separate status tables.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case: Cancel active order with no CONFIRMED shipments*\n- Read: Find order by orderId\n- Read: Find all shipments by orderId\n- Check: No shipment has CONFIRMED status\n- Write: Update order.status to CANCELLED\n- Write: Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n- Return: Updated order (200)\n\n*Case: Cancel already-cancelled order*\n- Read: Find order by orderId\n- Read: Find all shipments by orderId\n- Check: Order status is already CANCELLED\n- Return: Order unchanged (200, idempotent)\n\n*Case: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment*\n- Read: Find order by orderId\n- Read: Find all shipments by orderId\n- Check: At least one shipment has CONFIRMED status\n- Write: Nothing (transaction rolls back or never starts)\n- Return: ConflictException 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n\n*Case: Cancel non-existent order*\n- Read: Find order by orderId → not found\n- Return: ResourceNotFoundException 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n*Case: Create shipment for cancelled order*\n- Read: Find order by orderId\n- Check: Order exists and status is CANCELLED\n- Return: ConflictException 409 with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n- Write: Nothing\n\n*Case: Create shipment for non-existent order (existing behavior)*\n- Read: Find order by orderId → optional, not required\n- Write: Save shipment anyway (existing behavior unchanged)\n- Return: Shipment created (201)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n*OrderControllerTest:*\n1. `cancels an active order and returns the cancelled order` — POST /orders/O-1/cancel → 200, status=CANCELLED\n2. `cancels an order with only created shipments` — Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel → shipment status becomes CANCELLED\n3. `cancelling a cancelled order succeeds (idempotent)` — Cancel twice → second cancel returns 200, no error\n4. `returns 409 if order has a confirmed shipment` — Create order, create CONFIRMED shipment, try to cancel → 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT code, order stays ACTIVE\n5. `returns 404 if order does not exist` — Cancel non-existent order → 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\n*ShipmentControllerTest:*\n1. `returns 409 when creating a shipment for a cancelled order` — Cancel order, then POST /shipments → 409 with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED code\n\n**First line of code** comes after this phase marker, never before.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes in the order specified by the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":20247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1186},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9d5bac5-ee18-49f2-8c23-0f2e830ccfc9","uuid":"8a3f4267-25cc-447a-8e0b-51263f918447","timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:30:18.182Z","request_id":"req_011CevPhV2FcKw5X3AxH7t5L"}
